    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d528">

                <pb facs="0609" n="497" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg497"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/4478: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Commission to Negotiate
                            Peace</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-05-14T16:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 14, 1919, 4
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>1965. Following from Ambassador Morris:
                        <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“May 13, 1 p.m. Russian Ambassador has informed me that
                                Ivanoff-Rinoff has been recalled by the
                                Kolchak Government, claims,
                            being in my opinion a victory for general fusion [<hi
                                rendition="#italic">sic</hi>] which might form one of the grounds
                            for recognition of the Omsk Government.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>You will recall that Ivanoff-Rinoff was the Russian
                    Commander in Eastern Siberia who has been responsible for arbitrary and
                    reactionary policies which have been so much complained of by American
                    representatives and liberal Russians.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Polk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
